# Line endings are part of what the guards compare. Several tests byte-compare a
# committed file against `git show <sha>:<path>` or against a freshly generated
# copy, and the evidence pack records a sha256 of a written file. Git for
# Windows checks out CRLF by default, so on a Windows clone every one of those
# comparisons failed while the content was identical. Text is LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never normalised.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db   binary
